@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
title All AI provider calls through Redis / BullMQ
actor Administrator
participant "Feature orchestration\nLessons / Shared ideas / Model catalog" as Feature
participant "AiRequestQueueService" as Queue
queue "Redis\nllm-requests" as Redis
participant "BullMQ workers\nGlobal concurrency = 1 by default" as Worker
database "Provider settings\nMySQL" as DB
participant "OpenAI / Gemini" as Provider
Administrator -> Feature: Generate / revise / reprocess / list models
Feature -> Queue: Typed JSON or multipart request
Queue -> Queue: Validate endpoint / size / deadline
Queue -> Redis: Enqueue without provider credentials
Redis -> Worker: FIFO claim subject to global concurrency
Worker -> Redis: Check cached result / cancellation / expiry
alt Cached result exists
  Worker -> Redis: Complete with result key
else Request expired or cancelled
  Worker -> Redis: Fail without provider call
else Request eligible
  Worker -> DB: Read current provider credential
  Worker -> Provider: Execute request (bounded timeout)
  Provider --> Worker: Response or sanitized failure
  Worker -> Redis: Result key (5 minute TTL), clear job payload
  Worker -> Redis: Complete with result key only
end
Redis --> Queue: Completion event
Queue -> Redis: Consume result and remove terminal job
Queue --> Feature: Typed response / provider error / queue error
Feature --> Administrator: Existing feature status or response
note over Queue, Provider
Redis unavailable: no direct provider fallback.
Feature retry policies enqueue a new request for every retry.
Stalled work may recover; at-least-once delivery, not exactly-once billing.
end note
@enduml
